            <ArticleTitle>Phlegmasia cerulea dolens.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>401-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Phlegmasia dolens is a rare form of massive venous thrombosis of the lower extremities that is associated with a high degree of morbidity, including venous gangrene, compartment type syndrome, and arterial compromise. We report the sonographic findings in a patient who presented with phlegmasia dolens.</AbstractText>
